.SH NAME
Plack::Session::Cleanup \- Run code when the environment is destroyed
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
.Vb 5
\&  $env\->{\*(Aqrun_at_cleanup\*(Aq} = Plack::Session::Cleanup\->new(
\&      sub {
\&          # ...
\&      }
\&  );
.Ve
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
This provides a way for Plack::Middleware::Session to run code when
the environment is cleaned up.
.SH METHODS
.IX Header "METHODS"
.ie n .IP "\fBnew ( \fR\fB$coderef\fR\fB )\fR" 4
.el .IP "\fBnew ( \fR\f(CB$coderef\fR\fB )\fR" 4
.IX Item "new ( $coderef )"
Executes the given code reference when the object is \f(CW\*(C`DESTROY\*(C'\fR'd.  Care
should be taken that the given code reference does not close over
\&\f(CW$env\fR, creating a cycle and preventing the \f(CW$env\fR from being
destroyed.
